  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Medical Assessment Form (MAF) for Refugees Submitted for Resettlement from Uganda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This resettlement project aims to find long term durable solutions for refugees, mainly focusing on those who remain vulnerable (as determined by UNHCR) in the first country of asylum, Uganda. Refugees with medical conditions may be referred to IOM by UNHCR to assist with the completion of the Medical Assessment Form (MAF). The aim of the MAF is to identify refugees who need priority resettlement on medical grounds. IOM conducts an assessment of a refugee&apos;s medical condition, prognosis and the possibility of management in the country of asylum and provides recommendations on the need and urgency of resettlement.</narrative>
  </description>
